  "title": "She Kept Taking My Lunch. I Relabeled It.",
  "script": "Still missing? My name had been on the container in the office fridge for three weeks, then someone started eating half of it every single day and returning the empty tub. I switched to a locked lunch bag. Gone again\u2014bag and all. I bought the same yogurt, added two tablespoons of hot sauce only I could handle, and labeled it in huge letters: special diet, do not eat. Within an hour, our shared kitchen chat exploded with someone demanding to know who \u201cpoisoned\u201d the yogurt. I said nothing. She confessed first, mid-sentence, before anyone asked her name. HR got involved, and a sign-out sheet appeared on the fridge door within a day. My lunch stayed untouched for two weeks straight. Turns out one honest label was enough?",
